    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Start your Soho Open House adventure here!",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Designed by William Talman, clerk of works to Sir Christopher Wren, St Anne’s was consecrated in 1686, destroyed in 1940, rebuilt in 1990 and enhanced with an award winning re-designed entrance in 2016.  The new community coffee shop has fast become a meeting space for the community of Soho.  Massive and delicious croissants and superb coffee.  View the brand new timeline of Soho installed for Open  House Weekend, as well as the existing history of the church.",
                "Explore the historic gardens, relax on the terrace and plan your Soho Open House Neighbourhood adventure!"
            ]
        }
    ],
